        "transparentMax": 0
      },
      "colourManagement": {
        "displayDevice": "sRGB",
        "viewTransform": "Standard",
        "look": "None",
        "exposure": 0.0,
        "gamma": 1.0
      },
      "exrCodec": "ZIP",
      "note": "The binary mask and the emitted colour in one render. One sample per pixel with the box filter at its RNA minimum makes Cycles evaluate the same predicate a centre-sampling rasteriser does, because the integer raster coordinate is the pixel centre and the sample never leaves +/-0.005 px of it. A still costs one frame, so the full 1280x720 is affordable here where an animated case has to buy its grid."
    },
    "seed-shift": {
      "engine": "CYCLES",
      "device": "METAL",
      "resolutionX": 1280,
      "resolutionY": 720,
      "samples": 1,
      "adaptiveSampling": false,
      "denoise": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "pixelFilter": {
        "type": "BOX",
        "widthPx": 0.01
      },
      "filmTransparent": true,
      "filmExposure": 1.0,
      "scaleLength": 1.0,
      "bounces": {
        "max": 0,
        "diffuse": 0,
        "glossy": 0,
        "transmission": 0,
        "volume": 0,
        "transparentMax": 0
      },
      "colourManagement": {
        "displayDevice": "sRGB",
        "viewTransform": "Standard",
        "look": "None",
        "exposure": 0.0,
        "gamma": 1.0
      },
      "exrCodec": "ZIP",
      "note": "The same recipe with the sampler's seed moved. At one sample per pixel of a deterministic emission there is nothing for a seed to change, so any pixel that moves between these two renders is the oracle's own noise rather than a disagreement with us -- which is what makes this the instrument floor instead of an assumption about it."
    }
  },
  "notes": "A coverage case. Its shading -- textures, metallic-roughness, any extension it declares -- is NOT what this decides; board:1363 records why no case takes the shading arm yet. It carries BOTH keys the format allows in one file: twelve primitives name no material and take the reserved `<default>` slot, and the rest take an unnamed material's index. Modes that draw no surface put no pixel anywhere on either side.",
